<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$105.0 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$105.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The week's promissory note sales got off to strong start with a total of A$105 million worth of notes issued on Monday.</p>
<p>Mobil Corp's Australian unit led the charge, selling A$45 million of two-month notes at about two basis points over the corresponding bank bill mid-rate.</p>
<p>Dealers said there was moderate turnover during morning short end dealings with 90-day paper the most popular.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a little (two-way) business in 180s ... The one-month's are little slow,&quot; one discount securities dealer said. At 11.33 a.m. (0033 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.37, up four points on the day.</p>
